.Dd November 28, 2026
.Dt SERVERADMIN 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm serveradmin
.Nd manage this NextBSD computer for Server.app
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments
.Op Fl -json
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is what Server.app runs on each NextBSD computer it manages, this one
included, as root over SSH.
Every request is one typed subcommand with checked arguments, and every
answer is one JSON object on standard output; an error is
.Dl {"error": "...", "code": "..."}
with a non-zero exit status (2 for a usage error).
Nothing a caller sends is run as a command or used as a path.
.Fl -json
is accepted anywhere and changes nothing: every answer is JSON.
.Nm
refuses to run unless it is root.
.Pp
Updates go through
.Xr SettingsHelper 8 Ns 's
Update operations, the ones Update.app uses; everything else
.Nm
does with NextBSD's own tools:
.Xr zfs 8 ,
.Xr zpool 8 ,
.Xr bectl 8 ,
.Xr jail 8 ,
.Xr pkg 8 ,
the directory tools, and
.Xr dumpon 8 .
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm status
The operating system
.Pq Dq NextBSD ,
the protocol number, NextBSD version and build, the FreeBSD release the
system is synced to, host name, model, processors and their use,
memory, pools, the accounts role, the number of jails, the wired
Ethernet interface, and uptime.
Server.app refuses a computer whose
.Dq os
isn't NextBSD.
.It Cm pair Fl -add-key Ar key | Fl -list | Fl -remove Ar fingerprint
Server.app's ed25519 key in root's
.Pa authorized_keys .
.It Cm update status | check | download | install | cancel | restart
.It Cm update start-version Ar version | remove-version Ar version | keep Ar n
NextBSD updates and the installed versions (boot environments).
.It Cm users list | add Ar name Ar "full name" Op Fl -admin | password Ar name | remove Ar name | admin Ar name Cm on | off
Accounts.
.Cm password
reads the new password from standard input.
The last administrator can't be removed or demoted.
.It Cm quota set Ar user Ar size | Cm none
A space limit on the user's home dataset, such as
.Ar 10G .
.It Cm directory status | servers | promote | demote | leave | join Ar server
Share this computer's accounts, or use another's
.Pq Xr dspromote 8 .
.It Cm pool list | scrub Ar pool | scrub-stop Ar pool
.It Cm pool create Ar name Cm single | mirror | raidz Ar disk ...
.It Cm pool add Ar pool Cm single | mirror | raidz Ar disk ...
.It Cm pool attach Ar pool Ar disk Ar newdisk
Pools.
A disk must be one
.Cm disk list
reports as not in use.
.It Cm disk list
Disks not in a pool, not mounted and not swap.
.It Cm jailbase status | check | setup | upgrade | revert
The base system all jails share: FreeBSD's pkgbase set
FreeBSD-set-base-jail at the release this computer is synced to, in
.Pa <pool>/jails/base .
.Cm setup
also creates the datasets, makes bridge0 on the wired interface and
enables the org.nextbsd.jails launchd job.
.Cm upgrade
snapshots the base, upgrades it and restarts each jail once;
.Cm revert
returns to the snapshot.
.It Cm jail list | create Ar name | start Ar name | Fl -all | stop Ar name | restart Ar name | delete Ar name
.It Cm jail security Ar name Cm raw_sockets | sysvipc Cm on | off
.It Cm jail autostart Ar name Cm on | off
.It Cm jail name-check Ar name
.It Cm jail send Ar name | receive Ar name Cm move | clone Ar release
Thin jails: each is a dataset with its own
.Pa /etc ,
.Pa /var ,
.Pa /root ,
.Pa /home ,
.Pa /tmp
and
.Pa /usr/local ;
the rest of the base is mounted read-only with nullfs.
Settings are ZFS user properties on the jail's dataset
.Pq Va org.nextbsd.jail:* ;
the name is the dataset's name and the host name.
Each jail is bridged with vNET, gets its address by DHCP and announces
.Ar name Ns .local
with Bonjour.
A name is refused if this computer has a jail by that name or anything on
the network answers
.Ar name Ns .local .
.Cm send
writes a
.Ql zfs send -p
stream of the jail;
.Cm receive
reads one, and refuses unless this computer's base is the same FreeBSD
release.
.It Cm crashdumps status | collect Cm on | off | send Ar computer | Cm off | refresh | expect Ar computer | list
.It Cm crashdumps delete Ar computer | - Ar host Ar n
Kernel crash dumps over the network: one computer collects them with
.Xr netdumpd 8 ,
others send theirs with
.Xr dumpon 8 Fl s .
.It Cm log sessions | recent Op Ar n | search Ar word
Who is signed in, and recent system log lines.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/jails
the jail base and containers
.It Pa /Local/Library/Preferences/org.nextbsd.serveradmin.crashdumps.conf
the collecting computer this one sends crash dumps to
.It Pa /System/Library/LaunchDaemons/org.nextbsd.jails.plist
.It Pa /System/Library/LaunchDaemons/org.nextbsd.netdumpd.plist
.It Pa /System/Library/LaunchDaemons/org.nextbsd.crashdumps-refresh.plist
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr SettingsHelper 8 ,
.Xr dspromote 8 ,
.Xr jail 8 ,
.Xr netdumpd 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in NextBSD 27.0 for Server.app.
